+# Detailed Changes: Airflow 2.11.2 → 3.3.2
+
+## File: `requirements.txt`
+```diff
+- apache-airflow==2.11.2
++ apache-airflow==3.3.2
+```
+
+## File: `dags/inventory_snapshot.py`
+
+### Change 1: Task Function Signatures
+
+**`build_snapshot()` – BEFORE (Airflow 2.11.2):**
+```python
+def build_snapshot(ds=None, execution_date=None, prev_ds=None, ti=None, **kwargs):
+    as_of = execution_date + timedelta(days=1)
+    # ...
+    previous = _read_snapshot(prev_ds)
+    out = _snapshot_path(ds)
+```
+
+**`build_snapshot()` – AFTER (Airflow 3.3.2):**
+```python
+def build_snapshot(**kwargs):
+    context = get_current_context()
+    logical_date = context["logical_date"]
+    prev_logical_date = context.get("prev_logical_date")
+    ds = context["ds"]
+    prev_ds = context.get("prev_ds")
+    ti = context["task_instance"]
+    
+    as_of = logical_date + timedelta(days=1)
+    # ...
+    previous = _read_snapshot(prev_ds)
+    out = _snapshot_path(ds)
+```
+
+**Why:**
+- Airflow 3.0 removed positional parameter injection (`ds`, `execution_date`, `ti`, etc.)
+- Must use `get_current_context()` to access all execution context
+- `execution_date` was renamed to `logical_date` (semantic change in Airflow 2.2+)
+
+---
+
+### Change 2: `audit_snapshot()` Function
+
+**BEFORE (Airflow 2.11.2):**
+```python
+def audit_snapshot(**kwargs):
+    context = get_current_context()
+    day = context["execution_date"].strftime("%Y-%m-%d")
+    ti = kwargs["ti"]  # ← Got from kwargs
+    record = {
+        "day": day,
+        "sku_count": ti.xcom_pull(key="sku_count"),  # ← No task_ids param
+        "low_stock": ti.xcom_pull(key="low_stock"),
+    }
+```
+
+**AFTER (Airflow 3.3.2):**
+```python
+def audit_snapshot(**kwargs):
+    context = get_current_context()
+    day = context["logical_date"].strftime("%Y-%m-%d")  # ← execution_date → logical_date
+    ti = context["task_instance"]  # ← Get from context dict
+    record = {
+        "day": day,
+        "sku_count": ti.xcom_pull(key="sku_count", task_ids="build_snapshot"),  # ← Added task_ids
+        "low_stock": ti.xcom_pull(key="low_stock", task_ids="build_snapshot"),
+    }
+```
+
+**Why:**
+- Consistent context access pattern (all from `get_current_context()`)
+- Added explicit `task_ids` parameter to `xcom_pull()` for clarity and best practice
+- `execution_date` → `logical_date` semantic change
+
+---
+
+### Change 3: DAG Definition
+
+**BEFORE (Airflow 2.11.2):**
+```python
+with DAG(
+    dag_id="inventory_snapshot",
+    schedule_interval=timedelta(days=1),  # ← Deprecated
+    start_date=datetime(2026, 1, 1),
+    catchup=False,
+    default_args={"owner": "warehouse-ops", "retries": 1, "retry_delay": timedelta(minutes=5)},
+    tags=["inventory"],
+) as dag:
+    build = PythonOperator(
+        task_id="build_snapshot",
+        python_callable=build_snapshot,
+        provide_context=True,  # ← Removed in 3.0
+    )
+    audit = PythonOperator(
+        task_id="audit_snapshot",
+        python_callable=audit_snapshot,
+        provide_context=True,  # ← Removed in 3.0
+    )
+```
+
+**AFTER (Airflow 3.3.2):**
+```python
+with DAG(
+    dag_id="inventory_snapshot",
+    schedule="@daily",  # ← New parameter name
+    start_date=datetime(2026, 1, 1),
+    catchup=False,
+    default_args={"owner": "warehouse-ops", "retries": 1, "retry_delay": timedelta(minutes=5)},
+    tags=["inventory"],
+) as dag:
+    build = PythonOperator(
+        task_id="build_snapshot",
+        python_callable=build_snapshot,
+        # ← provide_context removed (context always available in 3.0+)
+    )
+    audit = PythonOperator(
+        task_id="audit_snapshot",
+        python_callable=audit_snapshot,
+        # ← provide_context removed (context always available in 3.0+)
+    )
+```
+
+**Why:**
+- `schedule_interval` → `schedule` (parameter name changed in Airflow 2.2+, enforced in 3.0)
+- `timedelta(days=1)` → `"@daily"` (use cron-style or preset syntax)
+- `provide_context=True` was removed from PythonOperator in 3.0 (context auto-available)
+
+---
+
+## Data Format Compatibility
+
+✅ **No changes to CSV output:**
+```
+sku,on_hand,change
+SKU-1001,83,
+SKU-1002,104,58
+SKU-3001,77,-1
+```
+
+✅ **No changes to JSON output:**
+```json
+{
+  "day": "2026-02-20",
+  "low_stock": ["SKU-1001"],
+  "sku_count": 5
+}
+```
+
+Replenishment team's alerting system will read the exact same format.
+
